    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "the problem isnt a shift in scenery. i look at the manuscripts and i see the peak. i don't want to see the decay. i don't want to be the old man struggling to remember a melody or watching my hands shake while I try to write. there's a certain dignity in leaving when the music is still beautiful, you know? before the silence becomes clumsy.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
