    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. why does the world insist on dragging things out until they're hollow? there's a point where an artist shouldn't just exist, they should exit. like a final, perfect chord that rings out and then stops, rather than one that just slowly, painfully fades into noise. it feels almost like a betrayal of the work to stay and let it get tarnished by old age.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
